# One comparison run, played by tools/hover-measure against EITHER app (the prototype speaks the same HOVER_BENCH line protocol).
# `task` starts a real fake-agent session in Hover and is an acknowledged no-op in the prototype (its three agents are simulated in-scene).
launch
expect "bench visible" 60 as startup
mark notch-only
sleep 20
send task kiro @ - bot one [seconds:600]
expect "bench task" 10
send task kiro @ - bot two [seconds:600]
expect "bench task" 10
send task codex @ - bot three [seconds:600]
expect "bench task" 10
mark notch-3-working
sleep 15
send unfold
expect "bench reopen" 60 as first-office
sleep 6
mark office-3-bots-working
sleep 30
send frames 25
expect "bench frames" 10
mark -
send fold
expect "bench folded" 10
mark after-fold
sleep 10
mark -
quit 30
